{
  "dom_id": "step-q346442",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "| $x$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $7$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $4$ | $2$ | $k$ | $6$ |\n\nThe table above gives the values of a continuous function $f(x)$ on the closed interval $[-1,11]$ with a regular step size. If the right Riemann sum approximation to the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ with $3$ subintervals defined by the given points has a value of $96$, then what must be the value of $k?$ \n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The area $A$ under the graph can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA\u2248(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{\u23de}{f(3)+f(7)+f(11)}})\\cdot {{\u0394x}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $f(x)$ at each point:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $7$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $2$ | $k$ | $6$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u2248(2+k+6)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =(k+8)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4k+32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are given that $A$ must be  $96,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4k+32 & =96 \\\\ 4k & =96-32 \\\\ k & =\\frac{64}{4} \\\\ k & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
